-- title:
--   Torsion bound for the degree-zero class group of a nodal curve
-- statement:
--   Fix an algebraically closed field $K$, natural numbers $n, m$, and a family $\bar F_0,\dots,\bar F_{n-1}$ of field extensions of $K$ each of which is a curve over $K$ in the sense of `IsCurveOver` (principal divisors exist for all nonzero functions, every place has residue field finite over $K$, and $\Omega_{\bar F_i/K}$ is free of rank one over $\bar F_i$) and is of essentially finite type over $K$. Fix gluing data: maps $s,t\colon \{0,\dots,m-1\}\to\{0,\dots,n-1\}$ and, for each edge $e$, places $x_s(e)$ of $\bar F_{s(e)}$ and $x_t(e)$ of $\bar F_{t(e)}$, where a place is a valuation subring of $\bar F_i$ containing the image of $K$, proper, and a principal ideal ring. Assume the hypothesis `hκ`: for every prime $p$ such that $K$ has characteristic $p$, every $a\in K$ satisfies $a^{p^N}=a$ for some $N>0$ (vacuous in characteristic zero). Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\neq 0$ in $K$ and let $k\in\mathbb{N}$. The group $G=$ `NodalPic0 K Fbar src tgt xs xt` is the quotient of the group of admissible tuples $(E_i)_i$ of divisors — each $E_i$ of degree zero and vanishing at every branch place $x_s(e)$, $x_t(e)$ — by the subgroup of those admissible tuples satisfying `IsNodalPrincipal`, namely tuples of divisors of nonzero functions $g_i\in\bar F_i$ admitting, for each edge $e$, a common nonzero value attained by $g_{s(e)}$ at $x_s(e)$ and by $g_{t(e)}$ at $x_t(e)$. The conclusion is twofold: the subgroup $G[\ell^k]=\{c\in G: \ell^k\, c=0\}$ is finite, and $$\#G[\ell^k]\cdot \ell^{kn}\ \le\ \ell^{\,k\left(2\sum_i \mathrm{genusFF}(K,\bar F_i)+m+\#\,\Gamma_0\right)},$$ where $\mathrm{genusFF}(K,\bar F_i)=\dim_K H^1(0)$ and $\#\,\Gamma_0$ is the cardinality of the quotient of $\{0,\dots,n-1\}$ by the relation generated by $i\sim j$ whenever some edge $e$ has $s(e)=i$ and $t(e)=j$, i.e. the number of connected components of the dual graph.
--
--   This is an upper bound for the order of the $\ell^k$-torsion of the generalized Jacobian of a nodal curve obtained by gluing the curves $\bar F_i$ along the prescribed pairs of branch places; after cancelling $\ell^{kn}$ it reads $\#G[\ell^k]\le \ell^{k(2\sum_i g_i + b_1)}$ with $b_1=m-n+c$ the first Betti number of the dual graph, as expected for an extension of $\prod_i \mathrm{Pic}^0(\bar F_i)$ by a torus of rank $b_1$, with only the inequality asserted. It is used in the torsion estimate [`AlgebraicCurve.natCard_torsion_tropicalPositionZero_mul_pow_le_of_semistableCovering_of_discFibres_of_rankOne_of_charZero_of_semistableModel`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.natCard_torsion_tropicalPositionZero_mul_pow_le_of_semistableCovering_of_discFibres_of_rankOne_of_charZero_of_semistableModel) for semistable models, and rests on the exact counts of $\ell^k$-torsion in $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of a single curve in characteristic zero and in positive characteristic.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_NodalPic0_natCard_torsion_mul_pow_le_pow_of_isAlgClosed.lean

